<item>
            <title>[LU-20814] l_getsepol: errlog() clobbers errno with ENOTTY</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20814</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In lustre/utils/l_getsepol.c, every error path calls errlog() and then does rc = -errno.&lt;br/&gt;
But errlog() calls isatty(STDIN_FILENO). When the kernel runs l_getsepol through&lt;br/&gt;
call_usermodehelper(), stdin is not a tty. So isatty() returns 0 and sets errno to&lt;br/&gt;
ENOTTY, and the real error is lost. Every failure is then reported as -ENOTTY (-25).&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
openlog(), vsyslog() and closelog() can also change errno.&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
Fix: save errno at the start of errlog() and restore it before returning.&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
Also in errlog(): the same va_list is passed to vsyslog() and then to vfprintf(). Reusing&lt;br/&gt;
a va_list after it has been consumed is undefined behavior. Use va_copy() for the second&lt;br/&gt;
call. This only matters when l_getsepol is run by hand from a terminal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Found while debugging &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20119&quot; title=&quot;RHEL/Rocky 10.1 selinux-policy drops kernel_generic_helper_t, breaking all Lustre&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20119&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20119&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
